# Upload exclusions for `railway up`. Takes precedence over .gitignore.
#
# This file exists because .gitignore lists two paths that are actually
# TRACKED and required at runtime:
#
#   app/portfolio/routes.py   <- imported by app/portfolio/__init__.py
#   sync_db.py
#
# git ignores those two lines (a tracked file can't be re-ignored), so they
# are harmless locally. Railway's uploader matches the patterns directly
# without consulting the git index, so it would drop both from the build
# context and the image would fail on `from app.portfolio import routes`.
# Listing exclusions explicitly here avoids that.

# Python
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

# Secrets — set these as Railway variables instead, never in the image
.env
.env_local

# Local-only app data
instance/
*.sqlite3
app.db
my_research_app.db

# Build artifacts — regenerated inside the Docker build
node_modules/
app/static/js/dist/
app/static/css/gen/
app/static/.webassets-cache/

# Local noise
*.sql
railway_backup_*
local_backup_*
*.bak
TODOs/
mockups/
docs/Screenshots_and_gifs/
